The LLM-facing vocabulary in SYSTEM_PROMPT (GroqClient.kt) is
  "none|stop|go|forward|backward|turn_left|turn_right|navigate"
and parseReply maps every one of those, so the prompt and the parser agree — this risk is REFUTED.
MainActivity's voice `when` tests direction.lowercase().contains("left"), not an exact
"left"/"right" match, so Turn("left") and Turn("right") both land.
What the mapping does NOT express: a Turn has no duration or angle. A spoken turn arms the
depth layer with PIVOT_LEFT/PIVOT_RIGHT, and the controller pivots on the tuned pair until
the centre is blocked or something else writes the intent - so a turn is ended by "stop",
not by a number of degrees. Backward is understood only so the app can refuse it out loud:

